# Monitor presets.
#
# A preset is matched against what a display reports about itself, never
# against the connector it happens to occupy. The same panel moved to another
# port still matches, and a different panel arriving on the same port does not.
# That is the whole point: this file names hardware, not slots.
#
# Anything with no entry here follows the general rule, which needs no
# configuration at all: the highest refresh rate the output can do, then the
# largest resolution available at that rate, at scale 1.
#
# Only scale is listed. Mode is computed, and position is left to Hyprland.
# Scale is the one value that cannot be derived, because it depends on how far
# the screen is from your eyes rather than on anything the connector reports.
#
# A machine-local ~/.config/hypr/local.monitors, if present, is read first and
# wins. It is not part of this repository.
#
# make|model|scale

# 14 inch laptop panel. At scale 1 the text is unreadable at arm's length.
# 1.5 puts it at an effective 1920x1200.
Samsung Display Corp.|0x419D|1.5
